    "_doc": "Crops the player sows on land they tilled on the inner map (systems/crops.js; ui/innerMapFarming.js). Each crop: its seed good (a GOODS entry in playerEconomy.json, sold in markets of the listed settlement types at qtyMult x population), the product good and yield range per tile, the growth days of each stage after sowing (sown -> sprout -> growing -> ripe; their sum is the days to ripen on a well-watered day each), the seasons it may be sown in, hardy (survives winter frost, growing at winterGrowth), water need (low/medium/high -> dry days it bears before it wilts), and the art of each stage on an LPC sheet ([col, row] in 32px cells; h: 2 for a sprite two cells tall, its row the lower cell). A day of rain or a watering counts as a wet day (full growth); a dry day grows dryGrowth. A ripe crop keeps spoilDays before it rots in the ground. Yield: a roll in the range x care (wet days / days grown, floored at careFloor) x the farming level's yield (data/skillPacks/food.json: also more dry days borne, frost days lived through, quicker work).",
